WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.980
You know, Lex Luthor may have been wowed by your high-tech smoke and mirrors, Dr. Grohl.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.980
But I've come to expect more hardcore evidence from boys and their toys.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.980
So far, my toys have provided a breakthrough in identifying the crystal's origin.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:25.980
Proved to me I wasn't wrong, spending weeks to lure one of Lex's top scientists out of hiding.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:31.980
After an exhaustive battery of tests, we discovered that the crystal's composition doesn't match any element on this planet.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:38.979
this planet. It appears to be some kind of computer hard drive. We believe it may be alien.

00:00:38.979 --> 00:00:42.979
You can't be serious. I know that's hard to accept, but that's what the facts support.

00:00:42.979 --> 00:00:48.979
No, the facts are Lex disappeared in an Arctic wasteland here on Earth. He's not lost in space.

00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:52.979
This crystal is the only clue that we have, so stick to science.

00:00:52.979 --> 00:00:57.960
Not science fiction, and find me, Lex Luther.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.960
Preliminary findings suggest that the crystal responds at a molecular level to sonic vibrations.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.959
If you allow me to proceed, this frequency generator,

00:01:06.959 --> 00:01:09.959
may be the key to telling you what you want to know.

00:01:09.959 --> 00:01:14.340
For your sake, I hope it is.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:02:03.799
I know the stock is crap.

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:05.799
But it's pump and dump time, my man.

00:02:05.799 --> 00:02:08.800
So hype it, sell it to make me profit, or you're dead to me.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.800
Hello. Hello.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:43.539
It came when I saw your Kryptonian beacon.

00:02:43.539 --> 00:02:50.259
Yeah. Whatever you say?

00:02:50.259 --> 00:02:51.259
I'm Maxima.

00:02:51.259 --> 00:02:53.259
Queen of Elmerach.

00:02:53.259 --> 00:02:59.360
I've been searching for you.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:02.060
I am, baby.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:24.439
Well, a little rush.

00:03:24.439 --> 00:03:26.439
What'd you give me?

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.439
A taste of things to come.

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:52.370
You're not Kryptonian.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.370
What's happening?

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:57.370
You're dying because you're not the one I came for.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:02.949
But I will find him.

00:04:02.949 --> 00:05:10.870
Ready for some breakfast for it?

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:16.660
You know, I still can't get used to just being you and me around here.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:45.339
Hello?

00:05:45.339 --> 00:05:47.339
I need you, Smallville. I just got to the planet, and I'm already here.

00:05:47.339 --> 00:05:49.339
the planet and I'm already having the workday from hell.

00:05:49.339 --> 00:05:51.339
What's your ETA?

00:05:51.339 --> 00:05:53.339
I'm flying into the building right now.

00:05:53.339 --> 00:05:54.339
I'll be there in a second.

00:05:54.339 --> 00:06:10.779
I thought you said you were coming in for a landing. What happened?

00:06:10.779 --> 00:06:12.779
Do you're running to some turbulence?

00:06:12.779 --> 00:06:14.779
According to the clock, I'm still two minutes early.

00:06:14.779 --> 00:06:15.779
Now, what's a hurry?

00:06:15.779 --> 00:06:17.779
Well, I need you to take on some of my workload.

00:06:17.779 --> 00:06:19.779
This is my second quarter of Java,

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:21.779
and I'm still not firing on all eight cylinders.

00:06:21.779 --> 00:06:22.779
Both night of sleep last night?

00:06:22.779 --> 00:06:23.779
More like no night of sleep.

00:06:23.779 --> 00:06:26.779
Jimmy moved in so he and Chloe can save their wedding pennies.

00:06:26.779 --> 00:06:28.779
But the groom snores like a freight train.

00:06:28.779 --> 00:06:32.779
I am so jealous of you in that Kent farmhouse all by yourself,

00:06:32.779 --> 00:06:34.779
so many empty rooms.

00:06:34.779 --> 00:06:36.779
It's pretty quiet.

00:06:36.779 --> 00:06:44.660
You are about as predictable as mullets at NASCAR.

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:49.660
One little mention of you living alone and you start singing the missing Lana blues.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:53.660
Now, I hate to be the one to dish out a helping of tough love here, Clark.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:56.660
But Lana is gone for good.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:00.660
Time to get back in the saddle, Buckaroo, but this go round, you need to look outside your wheelhouse.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:01.660
I didn't know I had a wheelhouse.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:02.660
I didn't know I had a wheelhouse.

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:06.660
Of course you do, pretty, friendly, damsel and distressy.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.660
You need to try another scoop of the 31 flavors,

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:12.660
maybe a little less sweet vanilla and a lot more wild cherry.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.660
Let's get back to the work.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:15.660
Please.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.660
Good idea. Very your heartache and your job.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.660
Here, start with this.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.660
Babyface broker dies of ticker trouble.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:26.660
How does a healthy 25 road suddenly die of a heart attack?

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:29.660
I don't have time to handhold, but the coroner's report

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:32.660
said the endorphin and adrenaline levels in his blood were sky high.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:35.660
You know, endorphins?

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:39.660
There are hormones that are released when the body performs a certain activity.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:41.660
Like when you play sport.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:44.660
Or there's another kind of activity two people share.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:47.660
Repetitive motion builds to a climax.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:51.060
Thank you.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:57.810
The police say they found the victim fully clothed.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:00.810
What, he didn't even get past first base?

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:03.810
And the M.E says the hormone levels weren't only through the roof.

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:06.810
They're higher than any normal human body can produce.

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:15.389
You know,

00:08:15.389 --> 00:08:18.889
Unpacking your fiancé really should be a wedding requirement course.

00:08:18.889 --> 00:08:22.889
I had no idea you had such a propensity for recording bass fishing shows

00:08:22.889 --> 00:08:25.889
