00:22:17.740 --> 00:22:20.740
The doctors say your vitals have stabilized, so you're going to be okay.

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:29.109
I need to know what happened at the ace of clubs, Jimmy.

00:22:29.109 --> 00:22:31.109
I almost spit all those cute shots.

00:22:31.109 --> 00:22:35.700
I know.

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:41.700
I know that you were with a woman, Jimmy.

00:22:41.700 --> 00:22:45.039
That that wasn't my fault, CK.

00:22:45.039 --> 00:22:47.039
I mean, the drinking part was, but...

00:22:47.039 --> 00:23:02.190
What you're talking about?

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:06.589
I found an old love letter that Chloe wrote.

00:23:06.589 --> 00:23:13.309
And I realized a person never really gets over their first true love.

00:23:13.309 --> 00:23:24.700
You believe you're gonna spend the rest of your life with someone.

00:23:24.700 --> 00:23:27.069
That they're the one.

00:23:27.069 --> 00:23:36.799
And when you gotta start over again with someone new, is it ever the same?

00:23:36.799 --> 00:23:47.539
Everyone has to move on, Jimmy.

00:23:47.539 --> 00:23:49.539
Chloe must have because she found you.

00:23:49.539 --> 00:23:55.950
You don't know how lucky you are to have each other.

00:23:55.950 --> 00:24:03.930
Woman, CK.

00:24:03.930 --> 00:24:08.670
It wasn't.

00:24:08.670 --> 00:24:10.670
your fault, Jimmy. You weren't in control.

00:24:10.670 --> 00:24:15.670
But I need you to tell me what she looked like, so I can find her before she hurts anyone else.

00:24:15.670 --> 00:24:19.670
Look, everything's a blur after she came up at me at the bar.

00:24:19.670 --> 00:24:28.240
Ginny, what happens, though?

00:24:28.240 --> 00:24:31.240
He's gonna be okay. He was at the Asa Clubs and things got a little messy.

00:24:31.240 --> 00:25:29.059
The important thing is that you guys are together.

00:25:29.059 --> 00:25:30.059
Clark Kent.

00:25:30.059 --> 00:25:34.589
That's a strong name. I like it.

00:25:34.589 --> 00:25:35.589
Who are you?

00:25:35.589 --> 00:25:42.789
Maxima. You don't know how long I've searched for you.

00:25:42.789 --> 00:26:09.940
You're not here.

00:26:09.940 --> 00:26:57.829
I'll take the stairs.

00:26:57.829 --> 00:27:06.000
Let her go.

00:27:06.000 --> 00:27:07.000
Close, wait!

00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:08.000
What?

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:10.000
Oh, sorry to rain on your Orgy Smallville.

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:12.000
I think I scared off your date.

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:13.000
Where'd she go?

00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:15.000
Probably to find you two in a motel room.

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:17.000
You don't understand.

00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:18.000
What's not to understand?

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:21.000
You're pulling a nine and a half weeks in the elevator.

00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:23.000
I mean, it may not get you a membership in the Mile High Club,

00:27:23.000 --> 00:27:25.000
but hey, you gotta start somewhere.

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:26.000
Just calm down.

00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:28.000
I am calm. I am perfectly calm.

00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:29.000
Why wouldn't I be calm?

00:27:29.000 --> 00:27:30.000
Dial down the ego, Smallville.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.000
I don't care what you?

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:32.000
do with your left life?

00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:43.619
Break.

00:27:43.619 --> 00:27:47.619
Does he really think I care who he sucks face with?

00:27:47.619 --> 00:27:51.569
Hello?

00:27:51.569 --> 00:27:54.569
That slutty Anna wasn't even his type.

00:27:54.569 --> 00:28:21.470
I couldn't kill you in front of him.

00:28:21.470 --> 00:28:24.470
But now that you're alone, I'll make sure you never take him away.

00:28:24.470 --> 00:28:26.470
Who, Smallville?

00:28:26.470 --> 00:28:30.470
Look, I don't know who or what you are, but you got it all wrong, lady.

00:28:30.470 --> 00:28:33.470
There is nothing romantic between Lois and Clark.

00:28:33.470 --> 00:28:35.470
You have a deep connection to him.

00:28:35.470 --> 00:28:36.470
I felt it.

00:28:36.470 --> 00:28:37.470
Then your radar's on the fritz.

00:28:37.470 --> 00:28:40.470
Fritz, because even on a good day, we're barely friends.

00:28:40.470 --> 00:28:42.470
You would never have been able to pull away from me

00:28:42.470 --> 00:28:45.470
if he wasn't drawn by his attraction to you.

00:28:45.470 --> 00:28:49.470
Look, he's about as attracted to me as a Red Sox fan to the Yankees.

00:28:49.470 --> 00:28:50.470
Well, you may not know it yet.

00:28:50.470 --> 00:28:52.470
But believe me, there's a bond.

00:28:52.470 --> 00:28:55.470
And I could see it on your face when you caught us together.

00:28:55.470 --> 00:28:56.470
You feel it too.

00:28:56.470 --> 00:29:01.230
But I finally found the man that I've wanted all my life,

00:29:01.230 --> 00:29:02.230
and you can't have him.

00:29:02.230 --> 00:29:03.230
Free!

00:29:03.230 --> 00:29:24.789
Just taught me through the face recognition software.

00:29:24.789 --> 00:29:29.579
I'll call you back.

00:29:29.579 --> 00:29:30.579
Amazing, Ken.

00:29:30.579 --> 00:29:34.579
It seems wherever we are in the universe, our stars keep crossing.

00:29:34.579 --> 00:29:35.579
It is strange.

00:29:35.579 --> 00:29:39.579
Especially when I find you in a locked office and you don't have a key.

00:29:39.579 --> 00:29:44.579
And how come Clark Kent has an all night pass to a clinic for the meteor impaired?

00:29:44.579 --> 00:29:46.579
My friend works here.

00:29:46.579 --> 00:29:48.579
She's helping me on an article.

00:29:48.579 --> 00:29:55.769
Are you writing a story about that woman?

00:29:55.769 --> 00:30:02.859
You know her?

00:30:02.859 --> 00:30:04.859
We had a close encounter this afternoon.

00:30:04.859 --> 00:30:10.509
What do you know about her?

00:30:10.509 --> 00:30:11.509
She's wanted for murder.

00:30:11.509 --> 00:30:16.059
It's a pretty big story.

00:30:16.059 --> 00:30:18.059
A big story for a copyboy.

00:30:18.059 --> 00:30:20.059
Up until now, she's only attacked men.

00:30:20.059 --> 00:30:23.789
I wonder why she'd be after you.

00:30:23.789 --> 00:30:28.539
She has her heart set on finding someone.

00:30:28.539 --> 00:30:36.019
Who?

00:30:36.019 --> 00:30:41.440
The guy who owns this.

00:30:41.440 --> 00:30:43.440
I was hoping that Chloe might use her

00:30:43.440 --> 00:30:48.940
skills to shed some light on it.

00:30:48.940 --> 00:30:50.940
Where did you get something like that?

00:30:50.940 --> 00:30:55.950
It was the only thing found at the spot where Lex disappeared.

00:30:55.950 --> 00:30:56.950
You spent a lot of time with Lex.

00:30:56.950 --> 00:30:58.950
Did you ever see him with it?

00:30:58.950 --> 00:31:08.859
Clark, do you know what this is?

00:31:08.859 --> 00:31:18.119
I've never seen that before.

00:31:18.119 --> 00:31:19.119
Yes.

00:31:19.119 --> 00:31:23.119
The target is located in his first circle, the corner of Melbourne and Holly.

00:31:23.119 --> 00:31:25.119
She flipped in a car.

00:31:25.119 --> 00:31:28.119
Civilian females trapped inside him on.

00:31:28.119 --> 00:31:35.349
Hello? What's going on?

00:31:35.349 --> 00:32:00.519
Bring it, bitch.

00:32:00.519 --> 00:32:03.519
I'm in with some fighting him.

00:32:03.519 --> 00:32:06.519
None of the men of my plan had a stamina to keep up.

00:32:06.519 --> 00:32:10.019
Maybe you shouldn't have come on so strong.

00:32:10.019 --> 00:32:13.019
You didn't seem to mind. You came back for more?

00:32:13.019 --> 00:32:16.019
I came back to stop you from killing Lois.

00:32:16.019 --> 00:32:17.019
What would you?

00:32:17.019 --> 00:32:20.980
done to her if I didn't stop you.

00:32:20.980 --> 00:32:21.980
I couldn't let her have you.

00:32:21.980 --> 00:32:22.980
You're my soulmate.

00:32:22.980 --> 00:32:24.980
You don't even know who I am.

00:32:24.980 --> 00:32:27.980
When I was a little girl, I heard the stories of the brave

00:32:27.980 --> 00:32:29.980
and gallant men of Krypton,

00:32:29.980 --> 00:32:32.980
men worthy of standing by a queen's side.

00:32:32.980 --> 00:32:36.980
When I learned your planet had been destroyed,

00:32:36.980 --> 00:32:40.740
prayed for survivors.

00:32:40.740 --> 00:32:47.410
I saw your beacon.

00:32:47.410 --> 00:32:48.410
The beacon didn't come from me.

00:32:48.410 --> 00:32:53.990
It doesn't matter.

00:32:53.990 --> 00:32:58.750
I found the last son of Krypton and

00:32:58.750 --> 00:33:00.750
you're everything I would.

00:33:00.750 --> 00:33:01.750
for.

00:33:01.750 --> 00:33:09.230
A man who is my equal.

00:33:09.230 --> 00:33:14.339
We kissed.

00:33:14.339 --> 00:33:24.019
I felt your passion so much stronger than I've ever felt from any other man.

00:33:24.019 --> 00:33:29.019
And I could sense that you were as desperate as I was to find a mate.

00:33:29.019 --> 00:33:36.180
You want me as much as I want you.

00:33:36.180 --> 00:33:42.150
I don't want you.

00:33:42.150 --> 00:33:44.150
Are you sure?

00:33:44.150 --> 00:33:48.150
Because no one on this planet will be a better match.

00:33:48.150 --> 00:33:49.150
I know.

00:33:49.150 --> 00:33:52.150
the loneliness of not finding your soulmate.

00:33:52.150 --> 00:33:56.150
You come back with me and you will never be alone.

00:33:56.150 --> 00:34:00.910
It's our destiny to be together.

00:34:03.599 --> 00:34:05.599
My destiny is here.

00:34:05.599 --> 00:34:07.599
And you're not a part of it.

00:34:07.599 --> 00:34:30.079
Oh wait.

00:34:30.079 --> 00:34:33.079
Hey. I just talked to the doctor.

00:34:33.079 --> 00:34:37.079
I'm bringing Jimmy home in two hours with his heart in the right place,

00:34:37.079 --> 00:34:39.079
and his hormones in check.

00:34:39.079 --> 00:34:40.079
I guess you figure.

00:34:40.079 --> 00:34:42.079
I figured out that Maxima kissed Jimmy.

00:34:42.079 --> 00:34:44.079
Oh, please.

00:34:44.079 --> 00:34:47.079
One look at Jimmy's blood panels and I put it all together.

00:34:47.079 --> 00:34:51.079
I can't say I'm thrilled that he maxed on an alien goddess,

00:34:51.079 --> 00:34:55.079
but I gotta say Maxima knows how to rev a guy's engine.

00:34:55.079 --> 00:34:58.079
You know, speaking from experience, he didn't stand a chance,

00:34:58.079 --> 00:35:01.079
especially since she went after him when he was vulnerable.

00:35:01.079 --> 00:35:05.710
He was really shaken up about some letter.

00:35:05.710 --> 00:35:08.710
Yeah, that letter was for you.

00:35:08.710 --> 00:35:10.710
I read it to you sophomore year in high school.

00:35:10.710 --> 00:35:12.869
We're in high school when you were really sick.

00:35:12.869 --> 00:35:15.710
The only way I have enough guts to tell you how I actually felt

00:35:15.710 --> 00:35:17.710
was when you were unconscious.

00:35:17.710 --> 00:35:31.519
I may not be the one you love today,

00:35:31.519 --> 00:35:35.519
but I'll let you go for now, hoping one day you'll fly back to me.

00:35:35.519 --> 00:35:40.539
The kicker is, you did respond with one word.

00:35:40.539 --> 00:35:42.539
Lana.

00:35:42.539 --> 00:35:47.130
I guess I always knew, I just...

00:35:47.130 --> 00:35:50.130
Clark, that was a long time ago.

00:35:50.130 --> 00:35:52.130
Don't worry, I don't feel that way now.

00:35:52.130 --> 00:35:55.130
I just wanted you to read it so that I could finally close

00:35:55.130 --> 00:35:57.130
that chapter of my life and put it behind me.

00:35:57.130 --> 00:36:02.440
Don't get me wrong, I don't regret having had those feelings.

00:36:02.440 --> 00:36:08.440
But that's because they helped repair me so that I was ready to share my love with the perfect person.

00:36:08.440 --> 00:36:13.329
And to me, that person is Jimmy.

00:36:13.329 --> 00:36:16.699
So you blew it, bud.

00:36:16.699 --> 00:36:20.340
I just want you to be happy.

00:36:20.340 --> 00:36:23.340
Clark, what you and I have, I will never share with anyone else.

00:36:23.340 --> 00:36:28.630
You're my BFF.

00:36:28.630 --> 00:36:32.630
Which is why, um, when Jimmy and I get married,

00:36:32.630 --> 00:36:35.630
I was hoping that you would give me away at the altar.

00:36:35.630 --> 00:36:38.630
away at the altar.

00:36:38.630 --> 00:36:40.909
Absolutely.

00:36:40.909 --> 00:36:42.909
I'd be honored to, Chloe.

00:36:42.909 --> 00:36:47.480
And I may have an early wedding present for you.

00:36:47.480 --> 00:36:51.480
Since Jarrell created Brainiac, I think he can cure your infection.

00:36:51.480 --> 00:36:56.480
Maybe so, but I thought that when the fortress disappeared, so did your father.

00:36:56.480 --> 00:36:59.480
Jarrell's just complex computer programming instead of kryptonian crystal.

00:36:59.480 --> 00:37:02.480
The same crystal that produced the fortress.

00:37:02.480 --> 00:37:07.820
And now Tess Mercer has it.

00:37:07.820 --> 00:37:09.820
That's the computer she wants me to hack into.

00:37:09.820 --> 00:37:10.820
And I think I can't.

00:37:10.820 --> 00:37:14.820
recreate Jurel and the fortress, I just need to get that crystal back.

00:37:14.820 --> 00:37:17.820
The only problem is I've already searched the Daily Planet and the mansion.

00:37:17.820 --> 00:37:18.820
I haven't found it.

00:37:18.820 --> 00:37:24.260
Maybe this time we use a little less brawn and a little more brain.

00:37:24.260 --> 00:37:33.590
I'll see you out, Ma.

00:37:33.590 --> 00:37:34.590
Don't it can.

00:37:34.590 --> 00:37:35.590
Zahai?

00:37:35.590 --> 00:37:38.699
Hey!

00:37:38.699 --> 00:37:44.090
Dito!

00:37:44.090 --> 00:37:45.090
Chuba?

00:37:45.090 --> 00:37:47.090
Do you kickbox, Chloe?

00:37:47.090 --> 00:37:50.090
I find it helps me focus my anger.

00:37:50.090 --> 00:37:54.090
Maybe I should rush over to the dojo, because I have a lot of it building up right now.

00:37:54.090 --> 00:37:57.090
Call me paranoid, but it sounds like that rage is directed at me.

00:37:57.090 --> 00:38:02.090
I don't appreciate people breaking into my office when I'm not around.

00:38:02.090 --> 00:38:04.090
Do it open.

00:38:04.090 --> 00:38:08.650
Do it again and I'll press charges.

00:38:08.650 --> 00:38:09.650
You made your point.

00:38:09.650 --> 00:38:17.329
Listen, while I'm here, maybe I could take a look at that supercomputer.

00:38:17.329 --> 00:38:23.599
Sorry, but uh, looks like the little hacker bird missed the worm.

00:38:23.599 --> 00:38:27.170
What do you mean?

00:38:27.170 --> 00:38:30.170
I thought you said that I was the only one capable of getting into it.

00:38:30.170 --> 00:38:33.170
You might be, but we won't know now because I don't have it.

00:38:33.170 --> 00:38:35.170
because I don't have it.

00:38:35.170 --> 00:38:39.280
It was stolen.

00:38:39.280 --> 00:38:41.280
Well, who else would want it?

00:38:41.280 --> 00:38:43.280
I intend to find out.

00:38:43.280 --> 00:38:45.280
Stay by your phone, Chloe.

00:38:45.280 --> 00:38:47.280
Only a handful of people knew about that device.

00:38:47.280 --> 00:38:49.280
When I find out who has it,

00:38:49.280 --> 00:39:13.099
taking it back.

00:39:13.099 --> 00:39:16.099
Hey, Lois, what are you doing here?

00:39:16.099 --> 00:39:20.099
You know, if you're worried about the editor taking away the story,

00:39:20.099 --> 00:39:22.099
buck up, it's not your fault.

00:39:22.099 --> 00:39:26.099
Metropolis PD says that, as far as they know,

00:39:26.099 --> 00:39:27.099
our big heritage.

00:39:27.099 --> 00:39:29.099
Bimbo has vanished off the face of the earth.

00:39:29.099 --> 00:39:32.099
I'm afraid this may not be the last we've seen of her.

00:39:32.099 --> 00:39:35.099
Hmm. Well, I'll be ready for her.

00:39:35.099 --> 00:39:38.099
The late night game of bumper cars might have knocked the wind out of me,

00:39:38.099 --> 00:39:41.099
but one supercharged Fembot can't put a serious dent in Lois Lane.

00:39:41.099 --> 00:39:46.590
Thanks for showing up when you did.

00:39:46.590 --> 00:39:51.289
I guess you could say you saved my life.

00:39:51.289 --> 00:39:53.289
Tell me about it.

00:39:53.289 --> 00:39:59.780
If I hadn't severed your love connection, you would have ended up like all her other days.

00:39:59.780 --> 00:40:02.780
You know, she said some weird things to me.

00:40:02.780 --> 00:40:03.780
Really?

00:40:03.780 --> 00:40:06.780
She said she was my soulmate.

00:40:06.780 --> 00:40:13.380
I think you can do a little bit better than a man-eating meteor freak.

00:40:13.380 --> 00:40:18.380
I know she's not the one, but it got me to thinking.

00:40:18.380 --> 00:40:23.199
Chloe showed me this love letter she wrote to me years ago,

00:40:23.199 --> 00:40:27.769
and her feelings were really intense.

00:40:27.769 --> 00:40:31.769
And Chloe was right there in front of me, and I never realized how she felt.

00:40:31.769 --> 00:40:37.389
What if my soulmate comes along and I'm too blind to see it?

00:40:37.389 --> 00:40:42.400
I don't know, Smallville.

00:40:42.400 --> 00:40:44.400
I think that when the right girl walking,

00:40:44.400 --> 00:40:51.980
that when the right girl walks into your life, you'll know.

00:40:51.980 --> 00:40:57.219
What would Maximus say to you?

00:40:57.219 --> 00:40:59.219
Nothing for the front page.

00:40:59.219 --> 00:41:03.219
Well, I gotta go. I'm meeting with a realtor, finding my own place.

00:41:03.219 --> 00:41:07.219
Those lovebirds are so sweet, my teeth will rot if I don't move out.

00:41:07.219 --> 00:41:12.219
Hey, Lois, um, you were right. This house is pretty big.

00:41:12.219 --> 00:41:16.039
If you want your old room back, it's yours.

00:41:16.039 --> 00:41:22.059
Being housemates didn't work out for us the first time, Smallville.

00:41:22.059 --> 00:41:24.059
I tempt fate.

